var FT={"Ace Pilot (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Piloting proficiency or Expertise, 1,000 ft Evasive Maneuvers, and soft crash landings.","full":"**Pilot Training.** You gain proficiency in Piloting. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Evasive Flying.** In the Pilot role, when you take Evasive Maneuvers you can move 1,000 feet in any direction.\n**Soft Landing.** Whatever the conditions, if you must crash land, you can set the ship down gently enough that nobody aboard dies.","fx":{"skills":["Piloting"]}},"Admiral":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Command several ships at once, up to your Proficiency Bonus or Charisma modifier.","full":"You can command more than one ship at once if each has a free Captain role, working communications and a crew that agrees to your command by majority. All ships you captain take their turns in the same round, in the order you choose. On your turn you can use your action to take the action the Captain role gives you for each ship under your command.\nThe number of ships equals your Proficiency Bonus, up to a maximum of your Charisma modifier (minimum 2)."},"Agent of the Tower":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Hidden tattoo, prestidigitation, disguised casting, and a short burst of quiet speed.","full":"**Tower Brand.** An invisible tattoo, seen only with detect magic, marks you as an Agent to other Tower members.\n**Cantrip.** You learn prestidigitation, or another wizard cantrip if you know it. Intelligence is its spellcasting ability.\n**Hidden Casting.** When you cast a spell, you can make an Intelligence (Arcana) check against DC 12 + the spell's level. On a success, you drop its verbal or somatic components (your choice).\n**Quiet Step.** As an action, muffle your movement for 1 minute. Creatures have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to hear you, and your speed rises by 5 ft. Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Member of the Tower"},"Android (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Immune to nonmagical disease, needs no food, drink or air, rests 4 hours inactive, and speaks machine code.","full":"You are an escaped android, a near-perfect copy of a human with wires and lights under your skin. You may not even know it.\n**Construct Body.** You are immune to nonmagical diseases.\n**No Needs.** You need no food, drink or air, though you can eat and drink.\n**Inactive Rest.** Instead of sleeping, you stay inactive 4 hours a day, fully aware of your surroundings. Sleep magic can still put you in torpor.\n**Machine Code.** You speak the native code-language of machines. You can use it to interact with arcane terminals and ship computers from range and to talk to constructs.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Aquatic":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Breathe air and water, and swim at your walking speed.","full":"Your world is almost all ocean, so you have gills, webbed fingers and toes, and fishlike scales.\n**Amphibious.** You can breathe water as well as air.\n**Swimmer.** You have a swimming speed equal to your speed.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"mv":{"swim":"speed"}}},"Archon (DM14)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Badge of rank, a bonus-action ally cover swap, and +1 to one save.","full":"**Badge.** You carry a badge of rank as an Archon of the S.S. St. Vincent. You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks to convince those who know it of your good will, and on Charisma (Intimidation) checks against raiders, pirates and other lawbreakers.\n**Step Between.** As a bonus action, place yourself between harm and an ally within 5 ft. Until the start of your next turn you take -2 to AC and the ally gains +2.\n**Steadfast.** Choose one saving throw. You gain +1 to it.","pre":"Member of the S.S. Saint Vincent"},"Artifactor":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Value and read magic items in a minute, attune to four items, and barter with Advantage.","full":"**Appraiser.** After studying an object for 1 minute, you learn its exact market value. If it is a magic item, you also learn its properties, how to use them, whether it needs attunement and how many charges it has.\n**Extra Attunement.** You can attune to four magic items instead of three.\n**Haggler.** You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks to barter, buy and sell goods and services.","pre":"Member of DD&D"},"Beastman":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Advantage on smell-based Perception and clawed unarmed strikes for 1d4 slashing.","full":"Short tail, coarse facial fur, long teeth and claws. You might look like any kind of beast.\n**Keen Nose.** You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n**Claws.** Your claws are natural weapons for unarmed strikes. A hit deals 1d4 + your Strength modifier slashing damage instead of the usual bludgeoning.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Blaster Roulette":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Add a matching pair of blaster damage dice to the damage again.","full":"When you roll damage with a blaster that has 2 damage dice and both dice show the same number, you can add that number to the damage roll."},"Blitzwarrior":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Reroll one Scatter blaster damage die, and close enemies no longer hamper ranged attacks.","full":"When you roll damage for a blaster with the Scatter property, you can reroll one damage die and must use the new roll. Also, having a hostile creature within 5 ft does not give you Disadvantage on ranged attack rolls.","pre":"Proficiency with simple blasters"},"Bounty Hunter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Perfect face memory, a 120 ft mark, and knock out targets instead of killing them.","full":"**Perfect Recall.** You remember the name and face of everyone you have met.\n**Mark.** As an action, mark a creature you see within 120 ft for 1 hour. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) and Wisdom (Survival) checks to find it, and you can tell whether it has passed through a place. Only one creature at a time.\n**Bring Them In.** When you reduce a target to 0 hit points with an attack or spell, you can knock it out instead of killing it.","asi":["WIS"]},"Cabal Broker":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Fire resistance (or cold if you have it), contract Advantage, and exhaustion for contract breakers.","full":"You are a bonded soul broker for the Cabal.\n**Infernal Dealings.** You have Resistance to Fire damage. If you already have it, you gain Resistance to Cold damage instead.\n**Dealmaker.** You have Advantage on ability checks to negotiate the terms of a deal or write a binding contract in your favor.\n**Breach Penalty.** A creature that breaks a contract with you or one you negotiated gains 1 level of exhaustion. Nothing can remove that level for 7 days.","pre":"Member of the Cabal","fx":{"res":["Fire"]}},"Chief Engineer (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Technology proficiency or Expertise, split shield power, easier ship repairs.","full":"**Engineer.** You gain proficiency in Technology. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Power Split.** When you drop the ship's shield to redirect power, you can send it to both the engines and a weapon, or to two weapons of your choice.\n**Fixer.** You have Advantage on checks to repair systems. A repaired system or weapon regains 5 mega hit points instead of 1.\n**Dry Dock.** When you repair the ship as a downtime activity, it regains mega hit points equal to three times your Proficiency Bonus + your Intelligence modifier for each day of repairs.","fx":{"skills":["Technology"]}},"Chosen Chaplain":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Religion proficiency, free worldseek, and a prayer that gives a crew member Advantage.","full":"**Religion.** You gain proficiency in Religion.\n**Worldseek.** You can cast worldseek once with no slot or components. Long Rest to use again.\n**Guidance.** As an action aboard a ship, pray for guidance. Choose one creature in a role aboard. The next attack roll, ability check or saving throw it makes as part of its role has Advantage.","pre":"Member of the Temple of the Chosen","fx":{"skills":["Religion"]}},"Coalition War Training":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Repeater and standard carbine training, 2d8 two-handed carbine shots, silent hand signals.","full":"**Weapon Training.** You gain proficiency with the repeater and the standard carbine.\n**Marksman.** When you attack with a carbine held in two hands without firing it automatically, its damage becomes 2d8.\n**Hand Signals.** Silent hand signals let you pass tactical information, such as enemy count, where allies should move and when to attack.","pre":"Member of the Coalition"},"Configuration Upgrade":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Reconfigure one score by +3, or three scores by +1.","full":"When you use Reconfigurable Ability Score Increase, you can raise one ability score by 3, or three different scores by 1, to a maximum of 20.","pre":"Vect"},"Decommissioner (DM14)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Spot disguised and infected constructs, reactive strikes, joint crippling, and bonus to saves vs technology.","full":"You recall defective constructs, hunt renegade androids and contain the N-Virus.\n**Construct Sight.** After 1 minute of watching or talking to a creature, you can tell whether it is a disguised construct. If it is a construct or living construct, you can tell if it is malfunctioning and if it carries the N-Virus, even a dormant one.\n**Counter.** When a construct or living construct within 5 ft makes an attack, you can use your reaction to make a melee weapon attack against it.\n**Cripple.** When you hit a construct with a melee weapon attack, you can cripple its joints. Until the end of its next turn its speed drops by 10 ft (minimum 0) and it cannot Dash.\n**Tech Resistance.** Add your Proficiency Bonus to saves against effects from magical technology, such as a concussion grenade or a volcanic."},"Depth Module":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Net, trident and spear training, 60 ft swim speed, and sonar blindsight in the aqua suit.","full":"An advanced depth module is built into your aqua suit. While you wear the suit:\n**Weapons.** You gain proficiency with the net, trident and spear.\n**Fast Swim.** Your swimming speed rises to 60 ft.\n**Sonar.** You gain blindsight 5 ft, which extends to 20 ft underwater.","pre":"Nautilid","asi":["STR"],"fx":{"senses":[["Blindsight",5,""]]}},"Doppel-Blooded":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Flexible Form fully copies a creature's appearance for 10 minutes.","full":"When you use Flexible Form to turn into a creature, you also take on its full appearance, as with disguise self, not just a vague copy of its shape. This is not magical and dispel magic cannot end it. You hold the appearance for 10 minutes, then revert to a vague copy.","pre":"Amoeboid race"},"Field Commander (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Order an ally to use a reaction action, and no Advantage against you near two allies.","full":"**Orders.** As an action, give an order to an ally within 60 ft that hears you. The ally can use its reaction to take one of these actions: Attack (one attack only), Dash, Disengage, Dodge, Help, Hide, Search or Use an Object.\n**Unit Tactics.** While you are within 5 ft of two or more allies who are not incapacitated, hostile creatures cannot gain Advantage on attack rolls against you.","asi":["CHA"]},"Firm Contractor":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"One skill from Data, Deception, Intimidation or Stealth, and Advantage on first-round melee against the surprised.","full":"**Training.** You gain proficiency in one skill of your choice: Data, Deception, Intimidation or Stealth.\n**Opening Strike.** On the first round of combat, you have Advantage on melee weapon attacks against any surprised creature.","pre":"Member of the Firm"},"Flexible Reach":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"10 ft reach, including Touch spells, and Reach on any melee weapon.","full":"You grow long pseudopods. Your reach is 10 ft, and Touch spells you cast have that range too. Any melee weapon you use gains the Reach property if it lacked it.","pre":"Amoeboid"},"Gambler (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Gaming set proficiency, Advantage on games of chance, and bet on damage rolls.","full":"**Games.** You are proficient with all gaming sets and have Advantage on ability checks for games of chance.\n**Stakes.** Once per turn, before rolling damage, place a stake: below the average or at or above the average. If you are right, add one extra damage die to the roll. If you are wrong, remove the highest damage die."},"Genius":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Four Intelligence-based skills and one rerolled Intelligence check per rest.","full":"**Scholar.** You gain proficiency in four of these skills: Arcana, Data, History, Nature, Religion, Technology.\n**Rethink.** You can reroll an Intelligence check and must use the new roll. Short or Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Intelligence 15","asi":[]},"Golem Upgrade":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Two scores +1, Charisma -1, AC 18 with Adamantine or Juggernaut Plating, no poison or sleep, spell save bonus.","full":"You embrace your golem heritage. You cannot take this feat if you have Vitality Upgrade.\n**Rebuild.** Raise two of your Strength, Dexterity or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20. Lower your Charisma by 1.\n**Plating.** With Adamantine Plating or Juggernaut Plating installed, your AC is 18.\n**Constructed.** You cannot be Poisoned and magic cannot put you to sleep.\n**Spell Ward.** Add your Proficiency Bonus to saving throws against spells.","pre":"Vect, Strength 17"},"Grax's Guy":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"One weapon or tool proficiency, and half proficiency on checks that lack it.","full":"**Training.** You gain proficiency with one weapon or tool of your choice.\n**Jack of All Trades.** Add half your Proficiency Bonus, rounded down, to any ability check that does not already include it.","pre":"Member of Grax's Guys for Cheap"},"Green Skin":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Advantage on saves against poison, Poison resistance, and unarmored AC 12 + Dex.","full":"Your people feed on sunlight through tough, photosynthetic skin.\n**Toxin Resistance.** You have Advantage on saves against being Poisoned and Resistance to Poison damage.\n**Tough Skin.** While you wear no armor, your AC is 12 + your Dexterity modifier.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Poison"]}},"Grue (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Darkvision 60 ft and re-hide when a Perception check finds you.","full":"One of your parents was a creature of darkness. Your skin is black and you cast a shadow in every direction, even in direct light.\n**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 ft as bright and in darkness as dim, in shades of gray.\n**Slip Away.** When a creature finds you while you are hidden with a Wisdom (Perception) check, you can try your Dexterity (Stealth) check again. On a success you silently move and it does not notice you. Short or Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]]}},"Hacker (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Data proficiency or Expertise, hack without a rig, and devices never lock on you.","full":"**Data Skill.** You gain proficiency in Data. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Rigless Hacking.** You can try to hack devices with no interface rig. With a rig, you hack as an action instead of over 1 minute.\n**No Lockouts.** Devices never lock after your hacking attempts.","asi":["INT"],"fx":{"skills":["Data"]}},"Hammer Rocketeer":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"2d4 thruster damage, double jumps with a rocket hammer, and a 10 ft push on heavy hammers.","full":"**Thrusters.** When you fire the thrusters of your rocket hammer, the extra damage is 2d4 instead of 1d4.\n**Uppercut Launch.** If you make a long jump or high jump as an action while holding a rocket hammer, you double the distance or height.\n**Shove.** Once per turn, when you have Advantage on an attack roll with a maul, rocket hammer, warhammer or wrenchinator, you can push the target 10 ft away on a hit. You do not need Advantage if the target is one size smaller than you or smaller.","pre":"Strength 13"},"Heavy Gunner (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Two blaster proficiencies, ship weapons crit on 19 or 20, and bonus damage dice.","full":"**Training.** You gain proficiency with two blasters of your choice.\n**Expanded Crit.** Your weapon attacks with ship weapons crit on a roll of 19 or 20. On a crit you choose which system is deactivated instead of rolling randomly.\n**Overkill.** When you roll damage with a ship weapon and two or more dice show their highest number, roll one extra damage die and add it."},"Iron Hero (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"+2 AC against higher CR foes, Advantage against whoever downed an ally, and cancel a legendary action.","full":"**Stand Tall.** When a creature with a challenge rating above your level attacks you, you gain +2 AC.\n**Avenge.** You have Advantage on attack rolls against any creature that reduced an ally to 0 hit points in the last round.\n**Intercede.** When a hostile creature you see takes a legendary action, you can use your reaction to stop it from happening. Short or Long Rest to use again."},"Laser Swordmaster":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Add Proficiency Bonus to AC vs blasters and laser blades, and max damage plus one roll on crits.","full":"**Parry.** While you wield an antimatter dagger, laser halfsword or laser sword you are proficient with, and a creature hits you with a ranged blaster attack or one of those weapons, you can use your reaction to add your Proficiency Bonus to your AC against that attack, which may make it miss.\n**Precise Crit.** When you crit with one of those weapons, instead of rolling its damage dice twice you deal the weapon's maximum damage and add its damage dice once.","pre":"Dexterity 13"},"Latent Psionics (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Six psionic power points to cast mage hand, minor illusion, command, disguise self, silent image and detect thoughts.","full":"A quiet hum of psionic power wakes in your mind. You have a pool of 6 psionic power points, regained on a Long Rest.\nYou spend points to cast spells. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability when you take the feat. It cannot be changed.\n0 points: mage hand, minor illusion.\n2 points: command, disguise self, silent image.\n3 points: detect thoughts.","pre":"Wrothian"},"Leviathan Suit (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Integrate weapons into your aqua suit, and shove through hostile spaces as a bonus action.","full":"You wear a Leviathan Suit, an advanced aqua suit given to nautilid warriors. While you wear it:\n**Integrated Weapons.** You integrate two one-handed weapons or one two-handed weapon into the suit. A drawn integrated weapon snaps into your hand and you cannot be disarmed of it. You can change them after a Long Rest.\n**Barrel Through.** As a bonus action, try to move through a hostile creature's space with an opposed Strength (Athletics) check. On a success you enter its space and push it up to 10 ft in any direction you choose.","pre":"Nautilid","asi":["STR"]},"Mantle of the Sun":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"A 1-minute divine transformation: radiant aura, crimson shield with resistances, or flight at 30 ft.","full":"You are a paragon of the Avia-Ra. You cannot take this feat if you have Nonbeliever.\nAs a bonus action, undergo a divine transformation for 1 minute. Long Rest to use again. Invest it in one ability. Aura: you shed bright light in 10 ft and dim light 10 ft further, and each creature you choose that comes within 5 ft or starts its turn there takes 1d8 Radiant damage. Shield: you gain +2 AC if you wield no shield, and Resistance to Fire, Necrotic and Radiant damage. Wings: luminous wings and a sunlike disk appear, giving you a flying speed of 30 ft.","pre":"Avia-Ra","asi":["WIS","CHA"]},"Mechanic (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Technology proficiency or Expertise, three tool proficiencies, and instant damage assessment.","full":"**Technology.** You gain proficiency in Technology. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Tools.** You gain proficiency with the circuitry kit, mechanist's tools and ship maintenance tools.\n**Damage Assessment.** You instantly judge the damage on any device you see: whether it can be repaired, how long and how much it costs, and what tools and materials it needs.","asi":["INT"],"fx":{"skills":["Technology"]}},"Nonbeliever":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Extra death-save failure, free darkness, and turn healing into damage.","full":"You are a heretic of the avia-ra and have turned from the Sun Above. You cannot take this feat if you have Mantle of the Sun.\n**Merciless.** When you reduce a creature to 0 hit points and it starts making death saving throws, it automatically gains one failure.\n**Darkness.** You can cast darkness once with no slot or components. Long Rest to use again.\n**Reversal.** When a creature you see regains hit points from magic, you can use your reaction to make it lose that many hit points instead. Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Avia-Ra","asi":["WIS","CHA"]},"Porterling (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Escape grapples and bindings with Advantage, and squeeze through tight spaces without penalty.","full":"You are the child of a human and a gnome or halfling, as tall as a dwarf but much leaner.\n**Flexible.** You have Advantage on checks to escape a grapple or slip bindings.\n**Squeeze.** You suffer no penalty for squeezing into a space meant for a creature one size smaller than you.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Precognitive (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Roll a d20 at turn start and use it to replace one roll, three times per Long Rest.","full":"You feel impressions of events a moment before they happen. At the start of your turn, you can roll a d20 and record it. The next attack roll, ability check or saving throw you make before the end of your turn is replaced by that number. You can do this three times, regained on a Long Rest.","pre":"Wisdom 13"},"Proto-Man (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Proficiency Bonus on saves against fear, and regain a Hit Die on a Short Rest.","full":"Your world has ancient fauna and colossal flora, and your people are hardy like very early humans.\n**Brave.** Add your Proficiency Bonus to saves against being Frightened.\n**Primal Recovery.** Once per day on a Short Rest, you automatically regain 1 Hit Die and can spend it right away.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Reptiloid (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Go twice as long without food or water, speak Draconic, and spit acid.","full":"You have rough skin, slitted eyes and a forked tongue.\n**Reptile Metabolism.** You can go twice as long as other humans without food or water.\n**Draconic.** You speak, read and write Draconic.\n**Acid Spit.** As an action, make a ranged attack against a creature within 30 ft. On a hit it takes 1d8 Acid damage per point of your Proficiency Bonus. Short or Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Roguean (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Cold resistance, immunity to harsh temperatures and space, and Darkvision 60 ft.","full":"You come from an icy rogue world flung from its star.\n**Cold Resistance.** You have Resistance to Cold damage.\n**Hardy.** Extreme temperatures in space and other harsh environments do not hurt you.\n**Darkvision.** You see in dim light within 60 ft as bright and in darkness as dim, in shades of gray.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"res":["Cold"],"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]]}},"Run and Gun":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Make a ranged attack as a bonus action after you Dash.","full":"On any turn you use your action to Dash, you can make a ranged weapon attack as a bonus action.","pre":"Proficiency with simple blasters"},"Scaleguard":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Intimidation and shield proficiency, and shield a nearby ally from damaging saves.","full":"You guard your charge whatever the cost.\n**Training.** You gain proficiency in Intimidation and with shields.\n**Take the Blow.** While you use a shield, if you and a friendly creature within 5 ft must both save against an effect that deals damage, you can use your reaction to give that creature Advantage on its save. You then automatically fail your own. If the creature would take half damage on a success, it takes none instead.","pre":"Member of Scale & Fang Inc.","fx":{"skills":["Intimidation"]}},"Showman (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Performance proficiency or Expertise, and a bonus from your audience, three times per Long Rest.","full":"**Performance.** You gain proficiency in Performance. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Playing to the Crowd.** If a non-combatant audience watches you fight, once per turn you can add a bonus to an ability check or attack roll equal to the audience size, up to your Charisma modifier. You can do this three times, regained on a Long Rest.","asi":["CHA"],"fx":{"skills":["Performance"]}},"Simian (2014)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Climbing speed of half your speed, and hold objects with feet and tail.","full":"You come from a world where evolution took a different path and your people look like monkeys or apes. You are just as smart as other humans.\n**Climber.** You have a climbing speed equal to half your speed.\n**Prehensile.** You can hold and use objects and weapons with hands, feet and tail, but you cannot make attack rolls with a weapon held by your tail.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Climber: climbing speed equal to half your speed"]]}},"Smuggler (DM14)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Piloting proficiency or Expertise, Advantage on undetected piloting and cargo lies, and a free first-shot reaction.","full":"**Piloting.** You gain proficiency in Piloting. If you already have it, add double your Proficiency Bonus to its checks.\n**Contraband.** You have Advantage on ability checks to pilot a ship undetected, hide cargo and deceive others about what it holds.\n**Shoot First.** When you roll initiative and are not surprised, you can use your reaction to draw a one-handed blaster and make a ranged weapon attack against a target in the weapon's range.","asi":["DEX"],"fx":{"skills":["Piloting"]}},"Spray and Pray":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Fire an Automatic weapon over a 10 ft cube, and use Strength for Mounted weapons.","full":"**Suppressing Fire.** As an action with a weapon that has the Automatic property, target a 10-ft cube. Each creature in it makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + Dexterity modifier) or takes the weapon's normal damage.\n**Mounted Strength.** You can use Strength instead of Dexterity for attack rolls with a weapon that has the Mounted property.","pre":"Proficiency with martial blasters","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Starguide":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Investigation proficiency, Advantage against space hazards, +5 to unassisted Blind Jumps, and immunity to Roach addiction.","full":"**Investigation.** You gain proficiency in Investigation.\n**Hazard Savvy.** You have Advantage on saves against natural hazards in space and harsh planets, such as radiation and high gravity.\n**Jump Charts.** Add 5 to rolls on the Blind Jump table for an unassisted jump. A result over 100 counts as 100.\n**Roach-Proof.** You are immune to Roach addiction.","pre":"Member of Astrogations Inc.","fx":{"skills":["Investigation"]}},"Strengthened Wings":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Fly at your speed in short bursts, and negate fall damage with your reaction.","full":"Your wings are larger and stronger.\n**Flight.** You have a flying speed equal to your speed. If you end your movement in the air, you fall.\n**Glide.** When you fall, you can use your reaction to slow your descent and take no fall damage.","pre":"Skathári","asi":["STR","DEX"],"fx":{"mv":{"fly":"speed"}}},"Sunstaff Master":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Dexterity for quarterstaffs, a bonus melee strike after ranged sunstaff attacks, and no Disadvantage with blasters near foes.","full":"You have mastered the sunstaff.\n**Agile Staff.** You can use Dexterity instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls with quarterstaffs you wield.\n**Two Ways.** When you take the Attack action to make a ranged weapon attack with a sunstaff, you can make a melee attack with it, as a quarterstaff, as a bonus action.\n**Close Fire.** You do not suffer Disadvantage for firing a blaster within 5 ft of a hostile creature.","pre":"Proficiency with sunstaffs, Dexterity 13"},"Swarmfighter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Draw or stow two weapons freely, double Foregrip range, and +1d4 on light one-handed blasters.","full":"**Quick Hands.** You can draw or stow up to two weapons when you roll initiative and whenever you take an action on your turn.\n**Long Reach.** When you wield a weapon with the Foregrip property in one hand, you can double its range.\n**Swarm Fire.** One-handed blasters you wield that have the Light property deal extra 1d4 damage on a hit.","pre":"Dexterity 13"},"Synaptic Bind":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Neural Lock stuns instead of incapacitating, and returns on a Short or Long Rest.","full":"You were an exceptional Taker who never let a quarry go. When you use Neural Lock, the target is Stunned instead of Incapacitated. You also regain the use of Neural Lock after a Short or Long Rest.","pre":"Wrothian","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Thermalsight Upgrade":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Thermalsight 60 ft through one foot of material, and see invisible creatures in range.","full":"You upgrade your optics.\n**Range.** Your thermalsight extends to 60 ft.\n**Penetration.** It passes through one foot of any material.\n**Reveal.** You see invisible creatures in range as if visible. This does not apply to creatures on the Ethereal Plane.","pre":"Vect"},"Thick-Shelled":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Unarmored AC 13 + Dex, and a d4 to bounce ranged spell attacks.","full":"You have a tougher chitinous exoskeleton than other skathári.\n**Shell.** While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 + your Dexterity modifier.\n**Deflect.** When a ranged spell attack would hit you, use your reaction to roll a d4. On a 4, the attack bounces harmlessly off your shell.","pre":"Skathári","asi":["DEX","CON"]},"Veteran Dogfighter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Dogfight as a bonus action with Advantage, survive at 1 mega hit point, and know ship models on sight.","full":"**Bonus Dogfight.** In the Dogfighter role, you can use the Pilot's Dogfighting action as a bonus action, spending half of the ship's movement. You have Advantage on the Dexterity (Piloting) check.\n**Hold Together.** In the Dogfighter role, when your ship would drop to 0 mega hit points, you can have it drop to 1 instead. Long Rest to use again.\n**Ship Spotter.** You instantly recognize any common ship model and know its usual passenger capacity, tonnage and weapons."},"Vitality Upgrade":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Gain a skill when you reconfigure a single score, and heal a free Hit Die on Short Rests.","full":"You embrace life despite your mechanical nature. You cannot take this feat if you have Golem Upgrade.\n**Learned Skill.** When you use Reconfigurable Ability Score Increase to raise a single ability score, you become proficient in one skill of your choice tied to that score until you take a Long Rest.\n**Self-Repair.** Whenever you take a Short Rest, roll one Hit Die without spending it and regain hit points equal to the roll.","pre":"Vect","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Warped":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM14","d":"Intimidation proficiency, and downgrade one critical hit to a normal hit per Long Rest.","full":"The lights of the Void have twisted you through radiation.\n**Unsettling.** Your face and body are hard to look at. You gain proficiency in Intimidation.\n**Shifted Organs.** When an attack that is a critical hit targets you, you can choose to take no extra damage from the crit, as if it were a normal hit. Long Rest to use again.","pre":"Near-Human, 1st level only","asi":["STR","DEX","CON","INT","WIS","CHA"],"fx":{"skills":["Intimidation"]}}};
var FTLU=[{"src":"feat","owner":"Agent of the Tower","feature":"Agent of the Tower","n":"Quiet Step","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Muffled steps, +5 ft speed"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Chosen Chaplain","feature":"Chosen Chaplain","n":"Worldseek","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Cast worldseek free"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Genius","feature":"Genius","n":"Genius Reroll","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Reroll an Intelligence check"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Grue (2014)","feature":"Grue (2014)","n":"Slip Away","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Re-roll Stealth when found"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Iron Hero (2014)","feature":"Iron Hero (2014)","n":"Intercede","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Negate a legendary action"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Latent Psionics (2014)","feature":"Latent Psionics (2014)","n":"Psionic Power Points","lvl":1,"max":6,"reset":"long","tag":"Spend to cast psionic spells"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Mantle of the Sun","feature":"Mantle of the Sun","n":"Mantle of the Sun","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Aura, Shield or Wings, 1 minute"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Precognitive (2014)","feature":"Precognitive (2014)","n":"Precognitive","lvl":1,"max":3,"reset":"long","tag":"Start of turn"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Proto-Man (2014)","feature":"Proto-Man (2014)","n":"Primal Recovery","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Short Rest"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Reptiloid (2014)","feature":"Reptiloid (2014)","n":"Acid Spit","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Ranged 30 ft, 1d8 acid per PB"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Showman (2014)","feature":"Showman (2014)","n":"Playing to the Crowd","lvl":1,"max":3,"reset":"long","tag":"Bonus = audience size, max CHA"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Veteran Dogfighter","feature":"Veteran Dogfighter","n":"Hold Together","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Ship drops to 1 mega HP instead of 0"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Warped","feature":"Warped","n":"Shifted Organs","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Crit becomes a normal hit"}];
